{{Quote|I was younger than you are now. I was a prisoner. They made a work camp in the jungle. No droids, no beasts, just men and cargo.|Saw Gerrera talking to Wilmon Paak about his time at the camp|<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" />}}
A '''work camp''' that operated in the [[jungle]]s on [[Onderon]] sometime before the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" /> The [[human]] [[Partisans|rebel]] [[Saw Gerrera]] was a prisoner at the camp sometime before he turned eighteen [[Standard year|years]] old.<ref name="Saw's age at camp">[[Saw Gerrera]] tells [[Wilmon Paak]] he was a prisoner at the work camp when he was younger than Wilmon is during the events of "[[I Have Friends Everywhere]]", which the previous episode, "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]" establishes takes place in [[3 BBY]]. And according to {{Databank|wilmon-paak|Wilmon Paak}}, Paak was sixteen [[Standard year|years]] old during the events of [[Andor Season 1|''Andor'' Season One]], which "[[Kassa (episode)|Kassa]]" establishes take place in [[5 BBY]]. Therefore, Paak was [[Reproduction|born]] in around [[21 BBY]] meaning that Paak is eightteen years old in 3 BBY. Saw must have younger than eightteen years old when he was at the work camp.</ref> During Gerrera's time at the camp, it operated with 200 to 300 individuals without the use of [[droid]]s or beasts of burden. Due to the extremes of the Onderon jungle the conditions at the camp were harsh and resulted in the workers clothes melting away thus forcing the workers to work naked. One day during his time there, there was a [[Rhydonium]] leak which caused everyone else in the camp, including the guards to run away. However the smell and itch caused by the Rhydonium was a new experience to Gerrera who became obsessed with it. Later calling it his sister when reciting the story to [[Wilmon Paak]] during a [[Rhydonium heist]] in [[3 BBY]].<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" />

==Behind the scenes==
The work camp was mentioned in "[[I Have Friends Everywhere]]," the fifth episode of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" /> on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref>

